codex
The changes introduce a missing B-roll reuse-registry entry and can leave an explicitly abandoned reel in the generated publication kit. Both issues can affect subsequent production or publication runs.

Full review comments:

- [P2] Register newly added B-roll in the reuse registry — C:\Users\NR SMART\tools\lcdg-reel-atelier\lcdg_1106\scripts_1106.py:205-207
  When a new block such as `B4.mp4` is added, it is absent from `par_fichier`, and this branch only checks whether the file exists; it never adds a registry entry. The plan therefore remains untracked and can be reused by a future episode.

- [P2] Remove the abandoned reel directory from the publication kit — C:\Users\NR SMART\tools\lcdg-reel-atelier\kit_publication.py:99-101
  When the script is rerun after a previous kit containing `13_Soins_chez_le_pharmacien`, that directory is never removed because the cleanup loop only visits the current `REELS` entries. The generated kit can therefore still expose the abandoned reel for publication.
